{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nimport itertools\n\ndef invnum(seq):\n    N = len(seq)\n    res = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            if seq[i] > seq[j]:\n                res += 1\n    return res\n\ndef naive(N, k, flag):\n    res = 0\n    for p in itertools.permutations(range(N), N):\n        for q in itertools.permutations(range(N), N):\n            if ((p < q) or (not(flag))) and (invnum(p) - invnum(q) > k):\n                res += 1\n    return res\n\nn, mod = map(int, input().split())\n\n# Use iterative DP with explicit table instead of recursion\ndef solve_iterative(N, k_target, flag_target):\n    # invnum for permutations of length up to N\n    max_inv = (N * (N - 1)) // 2\n    \n    # dp[length][k_diff][flag] = count\n    # We'll use dictionary for sparse storage\n    dp = {}\n    \n    # Base case: length 1\n    for k in range(-max_inv - 1, max_inv + 2):\n        for f in [0, 1]:\n            if f:\n                dp[(1, k, f)] = 0\n            else:\n                dp[(1, k, f)] = 1 if k < 0 else 0\n    \n    # Fill DP table\n    for length in range(2, N + 1):\n        invnum_INF = (length * (length - 1)) // 2\n        for k in range(-invnum_INF - 1, invnum_INF + 1):\n            for f in [0, 1]:\n                res = 0\n                for delta in range(-length + 1, length):\n                    if f and delta > 0:\n                        continue\n                    wt = min(length - delta, delta + length)\n                    prev_k = k - delta\n                    prev_f = (delta == 0) & f\n                    if (length - 1, prev_k, prev_f) in dp:\n                        res += dp[(length - 1, prev_k, prev_f)] * wt\n                        res %= mod\n                dp[(length, k, f)] = res % mod\n    \n    return dp.get((N, k_target, flag_target), 0)\n\nans = solve_iterative(n, 0, 1) % mod\nprint(ans)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint invnum(const vector<int>& seq) {\n    int N = seq.size();\n    int res = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < N; j++) {\n            if (seq[i] > seq[j]) {\n                res++;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nlong long solve_iterative(int N, long long k_target, int flag_target, long long mod) {\n    long long max_inv = (long long)N * (N - 1) / 2;\n    \n    map<tuple<int, long long, int>, long long> dp;\n    \n    // Base case: length 1\n    for (long long k = -max_inv - 1; k <= max_inv + 1; k++) {\n        for (int f : {0, 1}) {\n            if (f) {\n                dp[make_tuple(1, k, f)] = 0;\n            } else {\n                dp[make_tuple(1, k, f)] = (k < 0) ? 1 : 0;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Fill DP table\n    for (int length = 2; length <= N; length++) {\n        long long invnum_INF = (long long)length * (length - 1) / 2;\n        for (long long k = -invnum_INF - 1; k <= invnum_INF + 1; k++) {\n            for (int f : {0, 1}) {\n                long long res = 0;\n                for (int delta = -length + 1; delta < length; delta++) {\n                    if (f && delta > 0) {\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    long long wt = min(length - delta, delta + length);\n                    long long prev_k = k - delta;\n                    int prev_f = (delta == 0) && f;\n                    \n                    auto key = make_tuple(length - 1, prev_k, prev_f);\n                    if (dp.find(key) != dp.end()) {\n                        res = (res + dp[key] * wt) % mod;\n                    }\n                }\n                dp[make_tuple(length, k, f)] = res % mod;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    auto key = make_tuple(N, k_target, flag_target);\n    if (dp.find(key) != dp.end()) {\n        return dp[key] % mod;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    \n    long long ans = solve_iterative(n, 0, 1, mod) % mod;\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.35\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.794698856538162e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00011550712952157483, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.000563224486541003, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5809184312820435, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.8729025871143676e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.036001089960336685, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.01815405860543251, -1.537788011773955e-05, -0.21230381727218628, -0.02324649505317211, -0.6326252222061157, -1.3589766240329482e-05, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.22730368375778198, -0.2073204070329666, -1.811964830267243e-05, -0.18048010766506195, -7.510157047363464e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.6927575416048057e-05, -8.702239938429557e-06, -3.576272320060525e-06, -1.1920928244535